<%# Movies only, and only when the entry carries an id Letterboxd can resolve -- both
    conditions live in the helper, which returns nil otherwise.

    Points at the app rather than straight out to Letterboxd: the review prompt only
    exists at the canonical /film/<slug>/, and resolving that slug takes a request, which
    cannot happen once per card on a page of several hundred. %>
<% if letterboxd_reviewable?(entry) %>
  <a href="<%= letterboxd_review_path(entry) %>"
     target="_blank"
     rel="noopener noreferrer"
     class="letterboxd-link"
     title="Review <%= entry.name %> on Letterboxd"
     aria-label="Review <%= entry.name %> on Letterboxd">
    <i class="fa-brands fa-square-letterboxd"></i>
  </a>
<% end %>
